\title{NetClusterSim: Simulation Framework for Network and Cluster Interference}
\description{
The \code{NetClusterSim} package provides a flexible framework for simulating
potential outcomes, observed data, and true causal effects under
interference in both network and cluster settings.
}
\details{
In settings with interference, an individual's outcome may depend not only
on their own treatment assignment but also on the treatment received by
other individuals in their interference set. This package supports both
cluster-based and network-based interference structures under the potential
outcomes framework.

Specifically, for each individual \eqn{i}, potential outcomes are defined as
\eqn{Y_i(a_i, a_{N_i})}, where \eqn{a_i} is the individual's own treatment
and \eqn{a_{N_i}} represents the treatment assignments of individuals in the
interference set \eqn{N_i}.

The package implements simulation workflows for:
\itemize{
  \item cluster-based interference, where interference occurs within
  non-overlapping groups
  \item network-based interference, where interference is determined by graph
  connections
}

\strong{Main functions:}
\itemize{
  \item \code{build_network()} – generate a network object and node-level data
  \item \code{simulate_network_outcome()} – simulate network-level potential outcomes and observed outcomes under interference
  \item \code{simulate_network_true_effect()} – compute true causal effects under network interference
  \item \code{build_cluster()} – generate clustered population data
  \item \code{simulate_cluster_outcome()} – simulate cluster-level potential outcomes and observed outcomes under interference
  \item \code{simulate_cluster_true_effect()} – compute true causal effects under cluster interference
}

The package supports a complete simulation workflow:
\enumerate{
  \item define or generate the interference structure
  \item simulate covariates for each individual
  \item specify the treatment assignment model
  \item specify the potential outcome model
  \item generate individual potential outcome matrices
  \item simulate observed treatment assignment and observed outcomes
  \item compute true causal estimands from the potential outcomes
}

The outcome model can incorporate both individual treatment effects and
spillover effects through exposure mappings such as the proportion of treated
individuals in the interference set. Interaction terms between individual
treatment and peer exposure can also be included.

The package supports causal estimands under interference, including:
\itemize{
  \item direct effects
  \item indirect effects
  \item total effects
  \item overall effects
}

These estimands are defined as contrasts of average potential outcomes under
different treatment assignment and allocation strategies.

This package is designed to facilitate simulation studies for methodological
research in causal inference under interference across a wide range of
interference structures and data-generating mechanisms.
}
